.TH NVIM-SSH-CONTROL-OPEN 1 "2026-06-30" "termnav" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nvim-ssh-control-open \- open a remote Neovim target through an SSH ControlMaster
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nvim-ssh-control-open
.I host
.I target
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nvim-ssh-control-open
routes a remote file or link target through an already-open SSH ControlMaster
connection. It never starts a new authentication flow. Hosts must be explicitly
allowlisted, and the helper fails closed when the host is not allowed or the
master connection is unavailable.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERMNAV_SSH_CONTROL_HOSTS
Comma-separated allowlist of host aliases that may be contacted through an
existing SSH ControlMaster connection.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The remote target was opened.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 10
No existing SSH master connection was available for the host.
.TP
.B 11
The host argument was syntactically unsafe.
.TP
.B 12
The remote open command failed.
.TP
.B 13
The host was not allowlisted.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nvim-tmux-open (1),
.BR ssh (1)
